{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls7_jpg\\geo\\047.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "4.2PakistanisanAgricultural Country", "conf": 0.924, "box": [[76, 73], [515, 81], [515, 111], [76, 103]]}, {"text": "Climateof Pakistan,vastfertilefields along with theavailabilityof waterresources aresuitable", "conf": 0.924, "box": [[75, 111], [850, 119], [850, 147], [75, 138]]}, {"text": "for vast variety of crops. Various parts of country therefore produce many crops in abundance.", "conf": 0.938, "box": [[74, 137], [848, 145], [848, 171], [74, 164]]}, {"text": "Therole of agriculture in Pakistan economy is very important and it is considered the backbone", "conf": 0.908, "box": [[74, 163], [849, 169], [849, 196], [74, 190]]}, {"text": "of Pakistan'seconomy.", "conf": 0.885, "box": [[75, 191], [255, 191], [255, 214], [75, 214]]}, {"text": "In Pakistan, the most agricultural province is Punjab where wheat and cotton are grown the", "conf": 0.929, "box": [[73, 218], [847, 223], [847, 249], [73, 245]]}, {"text": "most.Themost important crops are wheat, sugarcane,cotton, andrice.", "conf": 0.921, "box": [[73, 246], [652, 246], [652, 272], [73, 272]]}, {"text": "4.4 Main crops of Pakistan", "conf": 0.889, "box": [[74, 277], [372, 276], [372, 303], [74, 304]]}, {"text": "Pakistanhastwocroppingseasons.", "conf": 0.925, "box": [[72, 315], [348, 312], [348, 337], [72, 339]]}, {"text": "i, Kharif season: It starts fromApril and lasts till September. Rice, sugarcane, cotton,maize,", "conf": 0.895, "box": [[67, 339], [845, 339], [845, 369], [67, 369]]}, {"text": "moong,mash, bajra and jowarareKharifcrops.", "conf": 0.927, "box": [[68, 367], [449, 363], [450, 389], [68, 393]]}, {"text": "i. Rabi season: It begins in October- November and lasts till April-May. Wheat, gram, lentil", "conf": 0.919, "box": [[66, 391], [846, 391], [846, 421], [66, 421]]}, {"text": "(masoor), rapseed, barley and mustard are Rabi crops.", "conf": 0.95, "box": [[67, 419], [509, 416], [509, 445], [67, 448]]}, {"text": "Othercrops"